{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And he sent his brothers.</b> Every form of the root לוה meaning 'escort' has a strong form (with dagesh), but when it means 'sending on a mission, to return,' it has a weak form (without dagesh)." "<b>Do not be agitated on the way.</b> Do not fear anything — [you may] bring all your livestock and your property and all that is yours, since you are my brothers, for I have peace on every side and the whole land is mine — like the expression לב רגז, 'an agitated heart.' Another interpretation: even though I loaded you with so much wealth in a time of famine, when highwaymen are plentiful, you need not be afraid."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:42.654614998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}